FCM setup (Android push) — REQUIRED before EAS production builds:

1. Firebase console -> create project -> Add Android app
   package: com.kendibo.app
2. Download `google-services.json` into `kendibo-app/google-services.json`
   (this file — same folder as app.json).
3. `app.json` already references it via
   `android.googleServicesFile: ./google-services.json`.
4. EAS: upload with `eas secret` or check into the private repo —
   NEVER commit it to a public repo.

Why: expo-notifications on Android delivers through FCM.
Without this file, `android` release builds fail at
`processReleaseGoogleServices` and push tokens are null.
Expo Go / dev: push is stubbed (see src/services/push.ts).
